       "name": null,
       "reasoning": "The task is to split a string into words where words are separated by commas or spaces. I need to handle both separators.\n\nThe simplest approach: replace commas with spaces, then split by whitespace.\n\nLet me verify with the examples:\n- \"Hi, my name is John\" \u2192 replace \",\" with \" \" \u2192 \"Hi  my name is John\" \u2192 split \u2192 [\"Hi\", \"my\", \"name\", \"is\", \"John\"] \u2713\n- \"One, two, three, four, five, six\" \u2192 replace \",\" with \" \" \u2192 \"One  two  three  four  five  six\" \u2192 split \u2192 [\"One\", \"two\", \"three\", \"four\", \"five\", \"six\"] \u2713\n\nThis works because Python's `str.split()` without arguments splits on any whitespace and handles multiple spaces.",
